# Android / Gradle
.gradle/
build/
app/build/
local.properties
*.iml
.idea/
.cxx/
captures/

# CodeAssist leftovers — NOT used on the PC build (see AGENTS.md).
# module.toml is CodeAssist's own project model; the real build is Gradle now.
# NOTE: the old `*.toml` rule was removed deliberately — it would have swallowed
# a Gradle version catalog (gradle/libs.versions.toml).
.platform/
module.toml
*.class

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Runtime logs written by the app itself. These are regenerated on every run and
# grow without bound; they are not committed. Packet captures that were handed
# over for analysis are different — they are evidence, they live in local/logs/
# and they ARE tracked.
*.log

# ==================== local/ — tracked for the move to PC ====================
#
# Everything in local/ is committed on purpose, to carry the working state from
# the mobile setup to the PC, so a fresh clone has the full picture:
#
#   local/logs/        packet captures and layout reports handed over for analysis
#   local/crashlogs/   crash reports pulled off the device
#   local/svgs/        the source SVGs the wear-icon drawables were traced from,
#                      referenced by comments in the drawables themselves
#   local/commits/     commit messages prepared on the phone (obsolete now that
#                      commits are made on PC, kept only so nothing is lost)
#   local/NEXT-SESSION.md   working session note from the mobile era. Historical.
#
# (local/notes/ was deleted during the move — its content was folded into
# AGENTS.md, PROTOCOL.md, ROADMAP.md and PACKET-CAPTURE.md.)
#
# Nothing here is ignored — there is no rule for it, other than the `*.log` rule
# above. To exclude something later, add a specific pattern rather than
# re-ignoring the whole folder.
